-- title:
--   Index of specialty at an attained Riemann genus
-- statement:
--   Let $K$ and $F$ be fields with $F$ a $K$-algebra satisfying `IsCurveOver K F`: every nonzero $f \in F$ has a divisor recording its orders $v(f)$ at all places and of degree $0$, every place has residue field finite over $K$, and $\Omega_{F/K}$ is free of rank $1$ over $F$. Assume the set of places $\mathrm{Place}\ K\ F$ is nonempty and that $L(0) = \{f : v(f) \le 1 \text{ for all } v\}$ is finite-dimensional over $K$. Let $\gamma \in \mathbb{Z}$ and let $D_0$ be a divisor with `RiemannGenusReachedAt γ D₀`, i.e. $L(D_0)$ is finite-dimensional, $\deg D_0 - \ell(D_0) = \gamma - 1$, and $\deg D - \ell(D) \le \gamma - 1$ for every divisor $D$. Then for every divisor $D$: the quotient of the adele space $\mathbb{A} = \bigsqcup_{E} \mathbb{A}(E)$ (the supremum, inside $\prod_v F$, of the submodules $\mathbb{A}(E) = \{\alpha : v(\alpha_v) \le \exp(E v)\ \forall v\}$) by the submodule generated by $\mathbb{A}(D) \cap \mathbb{A}$ together with the image of the diagonal map $F \to \prod_v F$ is a finite $K$-module, and its $K$-dimension $i(D)$ satisfies $i(D) = \ell(D) - (\deg D + 1 - \gamma)$, where $\ell(D) = \dim_K L(D)$ and $\deg$ weights each place by the degree of its residue field.
--
--   This is the adelic form of the Riemann–Roch theorem in the shape $\ell(D) - i(D) = \deg D + 1 - \gamma$, with the genus entering as an attained value of $\max_D(\deg D - \ell(D)) + 1$ rather than as a dimension of differentials. It serves as the input for Weil duality, for the identification of the space of Weil differentials as one-dimensional, and for the classical Riemann–Roch formula, and is used in the Čech-theoretic form [`AlgebraicCurve.cechRiemannRoch_of_genusReached`](thm.html#AlgebraicCurve.cechRiemannRoch_of_genusReached) and in counting arguments for effective divisors.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_AlgebraicCurve_indexOfSpecialty_eq_of_genusReached.lean

